    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0563" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851A.01/15: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at St. Pierre-Miquelon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pasquet</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">St. Pierre-Miquelon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-24T08:00:00-04:00">December 24,
                            1941—8 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Three Free French corvettes and submarine <hi rendition="#italic">Surcouf</hi>
                    under the command of Admiral Muselier entered early this morning to occupy St.
                    Pierre-Miquelon. No difficulties anticipated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pasquet</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
